      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "I'm inclined to say *no* to that, because all of her cards and powers that instruct her to change size simply say to \"switch\" her character cards---they don't mention anything getting destroyed or played. (Plus she remains the same target for any ongoing effects, such as Galvanise or Stun Bolt.)\n\nThis is supported by a couple of clarifications from [her wiki page](https://sentinelswiki.com/index.php?title=Sky-Scraper):\n\n[quote=\"Fireside Chats\"]\nSky-Scraper can swap character cards if Fixed Point is in play.\n[/quote]\n\n[quote=\"Fireside Chats\"]\nSky-Scraper is just one target, even though her character cards get switched.\n[/quote]\n\n[quote=\"Spiff's Clarifications\"]\nMany of Sky-Scraper’s powers say to switch to a particular character card. Switching character cards does not involve removing a card from play, nor does it involve destroying a card. You can never have more than one of her character cards in play at the same time. Sky-Scraper’s HP does not change when she switches character cards.\n[/quote]\n\nIf one wanted an unquestionably authoritative ruling, someone with the video game version could test this scenario out and see what happens.",
